XB-Kidux-Name-en: Expedition Code
XB-Kidux-Description-en: A coding game on its own website: children write JavaScript-style code to complete missions, alone or with up to two other players in a room. In English only, and in beta. Requires internet; it asks for no email and no password. Kidux is not connected with Expedition Code.
XB-Kidux-Name-es: Expedition Code
XB-Kidux-Description-es: Un juego de programación en su propia web: los niños escriben código al estilo de JavaScript para completar misiones, solos o con hasta otros dos jugadores en una sala. Solo en inglés, y en fase beta. Requiere conexión a internet; no pide correo ni contraseña. Kidux no tiene ninguna relación con Expedition Code.
XB-Kidux-Ages: 9-
XB-Kidux-Before: scratch
Description: Kidux learning module: Expedition Code, a door to the Expedition Code website
 Kidux is a Debian derivative for a child's first computer. This learning
 module opens the Expedition Code website, where children write code to
 complete missions, in a window of its own, and no other website: a link
 to anywhere else leads nowhere. Nothing of Expedition Code is in this
 package; the site and its missions are its author's.
 .
 It needs the internet. The site is in English only and in beta. It asks
 for no email and no password: a child chooses a name and an avatar, and
 the site gives a secret phrase to write down. Children may play in a
 room with others. The video the site opens with is on YouTube and does
 not play here. The package brings a font of emoji, which the site's
 avatars are drawn with.
 .
 Kidux and its author have no connection with Expedition Code.
 .
 Once it is installed, an adult switches it on for each child on the
 Modules page of the adult panel.
